# e2e run output. Screenshots are artifacts of a run, not sources; the site
# build consumes them from the run rather than from version control.
#
# Anchored to the directory that actually produces them. Bare `artifacts/`
# matched at every depth, so it also caught `packages/app/src/artifacts/`,
# which is real source. Git kept those files because they were already
# tracked, which hid the problem locally: the only consumer that noticed was
# `gcloud builds submit`, which falls back to `.gitignore` when no
# `.gcloudignore` exists and therefore uploaded a source tree with the
# artifact viewers cut out of it. Two production deploys failed on
# `Could not resolve "../artifacts/index.ts"` before anyone read the build log.
packages/e2e/artifacts/

# Site build output. Assembled by `bun run --cwd packages/site build`.
packages/site/dist/

# Terraform
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
